    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean that's a very linkedin-style way of putting it lol. but when you say critics worry about \"fragmenting the community\", isn't that just a fancy way of saying they're afraid of losing control over public funds? like, is the opposition actually based on kids' interests, or is it just about preserving the status quo for the institutions?\n volunty tell some real real real here,",
